<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech PVT Q1 1997 profit down.</title>
<headline>Czech PVT Q1 1997 profit down.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Czech data processor PVT a.s. said on Wednesday its net profit fell to 7.8 million crowns in the first quarter of this year from 56.1 million in the same period of 1995.</p>
<p>Results for three month ending March 31, 1997:</p>
<p>(in millions of crowns)</p>
<p> Net profit		  7.80	vs	 56.11</p>
<p> Operating profit	  8.65	vs	 62.90</p>
<p> Output		    281.62	vs	348.47</p>
<p> Total assets	  1,943.95	vs    2,156.47</p>
<p> Basic capital	   783.82	vs	785.82</p>
<p>NOTE: The company's shares are listed on the main market of the Prague Stock Exchange. Results are preliminary and according to Czech accounting standards.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
